pkg/terminal, service: restart by checkpoint note, rewind to restart stops, JSON prompt and checkpoints, generic names

restart NOTE, for a checkpoint made with checkpoint NOTE, fell through
to stock restart, which took NOTE as the program's new arguments: it
ran another program than the replay, from its start, with its output
no longer going to the -r files, and with no trace line at exit. In a
detsched program restart now runs to the checkpoint with that note, as
restart cN does, and refuses any argument that is not a checkpoint's
note or a position; restart alone still runs the program again from its
start with the same arguments and redirects.

rewind went back through the breakpoint stops only, so after restart
tD, a breakpoint stop, checkpoint and restart c1, it went to the
program's start rather than to the restart's stop. The stop of a
restart to a point, tD, sN or kN, is now a stop of the history rewind
goes back through, and rewind runs to the point again to reach it.

In the JSON mode the "(dlv) " prompt was printed before the next
record whenever the commands came from a file or a pipe, as at the end
of an --init file without exit, so that line was not JSON. The JSON
mode prints no prompt.

A breakpoint on a method of a generic type has addresses in its wrapper
for each type argument, (*T[string]).M, and in its body for the
argument's shape, (*T[go.shape.string]).M, both at the method's line,
and its confirmation named them alike, (*T).M(). It now names the
function of each address with its type arguments, and marks the
wrapper:

	Breakpoint 1 set at 0x49a1ca for main.(*T[go.shape.string]).M(), 0x49a26a for main.(*T[string]).M() (wrapper) ./main.go:13

The API breakpoint has the function of each address in Funcs, which the
JSON breakpoints record has as "funcs", and the error for a breakpoint
at an address another has names the address's function.

In the JSON mode checkpoint and checkpoints printed text, as output
records, which the filter the docs suggest drops. checkpoint prints a
checkpoint record, with the checkpoint's id, cN, note, when, and, in a
detsched program, its position and goroutine, and checkpoints a
checkpoints record with a list of them; the API checkpoint has the
position in Pos.

The restart and rewind changes and the checkpoints' positions are
detsched's (0003), the prompt and checkpoint records are the JSON
mode's (0003); the names of a generic function's
instantiations are a generic fix for upstream Delve.

